#lang saffron
;; saffron-dynamic-surface-pass M4/M5: a container held in an `any` reaching
;; a dynamic operator.  The compiled runtime panicked "no operator for a value
;; of that type" while the interpreter unboxed the Vec to its pointer and
;; printed an ADDRESS (println) or answered `false` for `=` on two equal maps.
;; Both now refuse by the box's name, in the same words: the dynamic surface
;; is a closed set, and a container is not in it.
(defn p [x] (println x))
(defn main [] : int
  (p [1 2])
  0)
